IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei4-part-vi-investigation-and-proof`

-- Tests of ei4-part-vi-investigation-and-proof.l4 (Act ss 124 and 125). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the
-- section; none is copied from the module's output.

§ `Fixtures: affidavits`

-- An affidavit that meets s 2(1) (sworn before a commissioner of oaths) and is the affidavit of a person acting for the Commission.
`a good affidavit` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
    `sworn or affirmed` IS TRUE
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS TRUE
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS FALSE
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS TRUE

-- Sworn before some other person authorized to take affidavits (s 2(1) accepts either kind of officer).
`an affidavit sworn before another authorized person` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
    `sworn or affirmed` IS TRUE
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS FALSE
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS TRUE
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS TRUE

-- Sworn, but before nobody the Act lists: not an "affidavit" under s 2(1).
`an affidavit sworn before nobody who counts` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
    `sworn or affirmed` IS TRUE
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS FALSE
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS FALSE
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS TRUE

-- A good affidavit, but the person who swore it does not act for the Commission.
`an affidavit by a stranger` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
    `sworn or affirmed` IS TRUE
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS TRUE
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS FALSE
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS FALSE

-- Not sworn or affirmed at all.
`an unsworn statement` MEANS `ei4 Affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` WITH
    `sworn or affirmed` IS FALSE
    `before a commissioner of oaths` IS TRUE
    `before any other person authorized to take affidavits` IS FALSE
    `the affiant is a person acting for the Commission` IS TRUE

§ `s 124(3) -- public notice and representations`

-- 124(3): a matter the Commission may investigate and means to investigate needs public notice.
#ASSERT `s 124(3) the Commission must give public notice of its intention to investigate the matter` TRUE TRUE
-- 124(3): a matter it is not empowered to investigate under this Act: no duty.
#ASSERT NOT `s 124(3) the Commission must give public notice of its intention to investigate the matter` FALSE TRUE
-- 124(3): no intention to investigate yet: no duty to give notice of it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 124(3) the Commission must give public notice of its intention to investigate the matter` TRUE FALSE
-- 124(3): representations from a person who appears to the Commission to have an interest, on a matter under investigation, must be received.
#ASSERT `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 124(3): a person who does not appear to the Commission to have an interest has no such claim.
#ASSERT NOT `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 124(3): nothing submitted, nothing to receive.
#ASSERT NOT `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 124(3): no investigation under way.
#ASSERT NOT `s 124(3) the Commission must receive the representations` FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 125(1) -- who may lay an information or complaint`

-- 125(1): an RCMP member, under this Act other than Part IV, may.
#ASSERT `s 125(1) an information or complaint may be laid or made by the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(1): a person acting for the Commission may.
#ASSERT `s 125(1) an information or complaint may be laid or made by the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- 125(1): neither: this subsection does not give the permission.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(1) an information or complaint may be laid or made by the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(1): an information under Part IV is outside the subsection.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(1) an information or complaint may be laid or made by the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(1): an information that appears to have been laid under the Act is deemed laid by a person acting for the Commission.
#ASSERT `s 125(1) the information or complaint is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(1) the information or complaint is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(1) the information or complaint is deemed to have been laid or made by a person acting for the Commission` FALSE TRUE
-- 125(1): only the Commission, a person acting for it, or a person acting for Her Majesty may call the informant's authority into question.
#ASSERT `s 125(1) the person may call into question the authority of the informant or complainant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(1) the person may call into question the authority of the informant or complainant` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(1) the person may call into question the authority of the informant or complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 125(1): the accused may not.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(1) the person may call into question the authority of the informant or complainant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 125(2) and (3) -- two or more offences, and territorial jurisdiction`

-- 125(2): a proceeding that relates to two or more offences is not objectionable on that ground.
#ASSERT `s 125(2) the proceeding is not objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences` TRUE TRUE
-- 125(2): one offence only: the subsection says nothing, so FALSE (it gives no such protection).
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(2) the proceeding is not objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences` TRUE FALSE
-- 125(2): a Part IV prosecution is outside.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(2) the proceeding is not objectionable or insufficient because it relates to two or more offences` FALSE TRUE
-- 125(3): a provincial court judge where the accused is resident.
#ASSERT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(3): where the accused is in custody.
#ASSERT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 125(3): where the accused carries on business, is found, or is apprehended.
#ASSERT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(3): the accused has no connection with the judge's jurisdiction.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(3): a judge who is not a provincial court judge as defined in the Criminal Code.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(3) the judge may hear, try or determine the information or complaint although the matter did not arise within the judge's jurisdiction` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 125(4) -- limitation of prosecutions`

-- 125(4): the Commission became aware on 15 March 2026; five years after is 15 March 2031.
#ASSERT `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2031 3 15)
-- 125(4): a prosecution commenced on that last day is in time; one day later is not.
#ASSERT `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 15) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2031 3 16) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 125(4): a prosecution commenced soon after the Commission became aware is plainly in time.
#ASSERT `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 125(4): awareness on 29 February 2028: the fifth anniversary does not exist in 2033, so it ends on 28 February 2033 (the keel's `add years` clamps).
#ASSERT `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2028 2 29) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2033 2 28)
-- 125(4): "other than Part IV": for a Part IV offence the subsection does not speak. NOT COVERED: NOTHING, not a date and not FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 125(4) the last day on which a prosecution may be commenced` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 125(4) a prosecution may be commenced` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2040 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 125(5) -- the certificate`

-- 125(5): a document appearing to have been issued by the Commission and certifying the day it became aware is conclusive proof of that day.
#ASSERT `s 125(5) the document is admissible in evidence and is conclusive proof of the day on which the Commission became aware` TRUE TRUE
-- 125(5): a document that does not appear to come from the Commission.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(5) the document is admissible in evidence and is conclusive proof of the day on which the Commission became aware` FALSE TRUE
-- 125(5): a Commission document that certifies something else.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(5) the document is admissible in evidence and is conclusive proof of the day on which the Commission became aware` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 125(6) to (10) -- affidavits`

-- s 125 and s 2(1): an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission, sworn before a commissioner of oaths.
#ASSERT `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` `a good affidavit`
-- s 2(1) accepts any other person authorized to take affidavits.
#ASSERT `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` `an affidavit sworn before another authorized person`
-- Not before a commissioner or another authorized person: not an affidavit as the Act defines the word.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` `an affidavit sworn before nobody who counts`
-- Not a person acting for the Commission.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` `an affidavit by a stranger`
-- Not sworn or affirmed.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125 the affidavit is an affidavit of a person acting for the Commission` `an unsworn statement`
-- 125(6): proof of personal service where all three statements are made and personal service is provided for.
#ASSERT `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(6): without the exhibit (c), there is no evidence of the request, notice or demand.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(6): without (a), the person has not said they have charge of the records.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `a good affidavit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(6): where personal service is not provided for by the Act (other than Part IV) or the regulations.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `a good affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(6): an affidavit by a stranger proves nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(6) the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` `an affidavit by a stranger` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(7): failure to file: the person was required, and the affidavit says the records were searched and nothing was found.
#ASSERT `s 125(7) the affidavit is evidence that in that case the person did not file or make the return, statement, answer or certificate` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(7) the affidavit is evidence that in that case the person did not file or make the return, statement, answer or certificate` `a good affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(7) the affidavit is evidence that in that case the person did not file or make the return, statement, answer or certificate` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(8): time of compliance.
#ASSERT `s 125(8) the affidavit is evidence that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on that day and not before` `an affidavit sworn before another authorized person` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(8) the affidavit is evidence that the return, statement, answer or certificate was filed or made on that day and not before` `an affidavit sworn before nobody who counts` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(9): proof of documents.
#ASSERT `s 125(9) the affidavit is evidence of the nature and contents of the document and is admissible with the same probative force as the original` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(9) the affidavit is evidence of the nature and contents of the document and is admissible with the same probative force as the original` `a good affidavit` TRUE FALSE
-- 125(10): where the affidavit shows the affiant acts for the Commission, no proof of the signatures or of that fact is needed.
#ASSERT `s 125(10) it is not necessary to prove the signature, that the person is acting for the Commission, or the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(10) it is not necessary to prove the signature, that the person is acting for the Commission, or the signature or official character of the person before whom the affidavit was sworn` FALSE

§ `s 125(11) to (14) -- judicial notice, deemed documents and forms, proof of return`

-- 125(11): judicial notice of orders under the Act other than Part IV.
#ASSERT `s 125(11) judicial notice shall be taken of the order without its being specially pleaded or proven` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(11) judicial notice shall be taken of the order without its being specially pleaded or proven` FALSE
-- 125(12): a document that appears to be an order, executed under the Act, over the Commission's name, and not called into question.
#ASSERT `s 125(12) the document is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Commission or the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(12): once the Commission (or someone acting for it or for Her Majesty) calls it into question, the deeming stops.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(12) the document is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Commission or the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(12): not over the name of the Commission or a person acting for it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(12) the document is deemed to be a document signed, made and issued by the Commission or the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(13): a form that appears to be authorized is deemed authorized unless called into question.
#ASSERT `s 125(13) the form is deemed to be a form authorized by the Commission under this Act other than Part IV` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(13) the form is deemed to be a form authorized by the Commission under this Act other than Part IV` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(13) the form is deemed to be a form authorized by the Commission under this Act other than Part IV` FALSE FALSE
-- 125(14): a return that appears to have been filed by or for the accused is proof that it was, absent evidence to the contrary.
#ASSERT `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(14): one that appears to have been made or signed by or for the accused.
#ASSERT `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- 125(14): evidence to the contrary defeats the proof.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(14): it does not appear to be the accused's.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(14) the production of the document is proof that it was filed or delivered by or for, or made or signed by or for, the person charged` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 125(15) and (16) -- repealed subsection, and proof of records`

#EVAL `s 125(15) repealed, and therefore not encoded`
-- 125(16): in a prosecution for an offence under this Act (no "other than Part IV"), the affidavit about unremitted amounts is evidence.
#ASSERT `s 125(16) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(16) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` `a good affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(16) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` `an unsworn statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(16) the affidavit is evidence of the statements contained in it` `a good affidavit` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `s 125(17) -- officers, directors and agents of corporations`

-- 125(17): an officer who directed the offence.
#ASSERT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(17): authorized, assented to, acquiesced in, or participated in: each is enough.
#ASSERT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 125(17): an officer who did none of the five things is not caught by this subsection.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- 125(17): a person who is not an officer, director or agent.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 125(17): the corporation committed no offence under this Act other than Part IV.
#ASSERT NOT `s 125(17) the officer, director or agent is a party to and guilty of the offence and liable on conviction to the punishment provided for it` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
